2026-09-27T11:11:24.4048054Z Reporting Issues
2026-09-27T11:11:24.4048259Z ================
2026-09-27T11:11:24.4048370Z 
2026-09-27T11:11:24.4048520Z Issues can be reported in the master issue tracker at:
2026-09-27T11:11:24.4048861Z https://github.com/deadsnakes/issues/issues
2026-09-27T11:11:24.4049079Z 
2026-09-27T11:11:24.4049181Z Supported Ubuntu and Python Versions
2026-09-27T11:11:24.4049438Z ====================================
2026-09-27T11:11:24.4049600Z 
2026-09-27T11:11:24.4049729Z - Ubuntu 22.04 (jammy) Python3.7+ (NOT Python3.10)
2026-09-27T11:11:24.4050144Z - Ubuntu 24.04 (noble) Python3.7+ (NOT Python3.12)
2026-09-27T11:11:24.4050473Z - Ubuntu 26.04 (resolute) Python3.7+ (NOT Python3.14)
2026-09-27T11:11:24.4051109Z - Note: Python 3.10 (jammy), Python3.12 (noble), Python3.14 (resolute) are not provided by deadsnakes as upstream ubuntu provides those packages.
2026-09-27T11:11:24.4051610Z 
2026-09-27T11:11:24.4051714Z Why some packages aren't built:
2026-09-27T11:11:24.4052107Z - Note: for 22.04+, older python versions requre libssl<3 so they are not currently built
2026-09-27T11:11:24.4052609Z - If you need these, reach out to asottile to set up a private ppa
2026-09-27T11:11:24.4052880Z 
2026-09-27T11:11:24.4858183Z The packages may also work on other versions of Ubuntu or Debian, but that is not tested or supported.
2026-09-27T11:11:24.4858935Z 
2026-09-27T11:11:24.4859085Z Packages
2026-09-27T11:11:24.4859398Z ========
2026-09-27T11:11:24.4859577Z 
2026-09-27T11:11:24.4861978Z The packages provided here are loosely based on the debian upstream packages with some modifications to make them more usable as non-default pythons and on ubuntu.  As such, the packages follow debian's patterns and often do not include a full python distribution with just `apt install python#.#`.  Here is a list of packages that may be useful along with the default install:
2026-09-27T11:11:24.4864495Z 
2026-09-27T11:11:24.4864950Z - `python#.#-dev`: includes development headers for building C extensions
2026-09-27T11:11:24.4865982Z - `python#.#-venv`: provides the standard library `venv` module
2026-09-27T11:11:24.4868327Z - `python#.#-distutils`: provides the standard library `distutils` module
2026-09-27T11:11:24.4869411Z - `python#.#-lib2to3`: provides the `2to3-#.#` utility as well as the standard library `lib2to3` module
2026-09-27T11:11:24.4954342Z - `python#.#-gdbm`: provides the standard library `dbm.gnu` module
2026-09-27T11:11:24.4955240Z - `python#.#-tk`: provides the standard library `tkinter` module
2026-09-27T11:11:24.4956224Z 
2026-09-27T11:11:24.4956400Z Third-Party Python Modules
2026-09-27T11:11:24.4956779Z ==========================
2026-09-27T11:11:24.4956985Z 
2026-09-27T11:11:24.4958868Z Python modules in the official Ubuntu repositories are packaged to work with the Python interpreters from the official repositories. Accordingly, they generally won't work with the Python interpreters from this PPA. As an exception, pure-Python modules for Python 3 will work, but any compiled extension modules won't.
2026-09-27T11:11:24.4960648Z 
2026-09-27T11:11:24.4961646Z To install 3rd-party Python modules, you should use the common Python packaging tools.  For an introduction into the Python packaging ecosystem and its tools, refer to the Python Packaging User Guide:
2026-09-27T11:11:24.4962937Z https://packaging.python.org/installing/
2026-09-27T11:11:24.4963240Z 
